    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of validations and side-effects applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The path is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, but almost all logic lives in a stack of `@ControllerAdvice` beans that fire *around* the controller, plus the mapper and service.\n\n## 1. Security gate (filter chain)\n- **By default: none.** `application.properties` has `petclinic.security.enable=false`, so `DisableSecurityConfig` (`permitAll`, no method security) is active and the controller's `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` is a **no-op**.\n- Only if `petclinic.security.enable=true` does `BasicAuthenticationConfig` load, requiring HTTP Basic auth + `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n## 2. `beforeBodyRead` \u2014 on the raw JSON, before deserialization\n- **`OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice`**: derives `householdId = Households.id(lastName, postcode)` (SHA-256) and **injects it into the request body** (side-effect \u2014 overwrites any client-supplied `householdId`). Then, unless the JSON carries `sharesHousehold=true`, if an existing owner already has that householdId \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 3. Jackson deserializes the body into `OwnerFieldsDto`\n\n## 4. `afterBodyRead` \u2014 after deserialization, before `@Valid` (order among these is nondeterministic; first match short-circuits)\n- **`OwnerRequiredFieldsAdvice`** (create+update): firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone null-or-blank \u2192 **400** (`{\"errors\":[...]}`).\n- **`OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice`** (create+update): email domain in {mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com} \u2192 **400**.\n- **`OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`**: city already has \u226550 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n- **`OwnerDailyLimitAdvice`**: \u2265100 owners already registered today (business-day-adjusted) \u2192 **429**.\n- **`OwnerPostcodeAdvice`**: 4-digit postcode outside its city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any) \u2192 **400**.\n- **`OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`**: supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 **400**.\n- **`OwnerTelephoneLengthAdvice`**: normalized E.164 national-number length wrong for country code (`+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 **400**.\n- **`OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice` (afterBodyRead)**: recomputes `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId` and compares against every existing owner \u2192 duplicate \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 5. `@Valid` Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`\nEnforced now (failures \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`):\n- **firstName**: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/'/-separated words)\n- **lastName**: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (like firstName, trailing `.` allowed)\n- **address**: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n- **city**: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n- **telephone**: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`, `@Pattern` requiring exactly 10 digits\n- **email** (optional): `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email`\n- **postcode** (optional): `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n- registrationDate / birthDate: `@Valid` LocalDate\n\n## 6. Controller \u2192 `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` (mapping side-effects)\n- `telephone` normalized to E.164 (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164` \u2014 strips non-digits, assumes `+61`, drops leading 0)\n- `address` normalized via entity setter (`AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse spaces, UPPERCASE, expand ST\u2192STREET/RD\u2192ROAD/AVE\u2192AVENUE)\n- `email` lower-cased (entity setter)\n- `registrationDate` = supplied date else `LocalDate.now()`, then rolled to next business day (`BusinessDays.toBusinessDay`)\n- `householdId` carried through from the value injected in step 2; `id` and `pets` ignored\n\n## 7. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 `@Transactional` side-effects (only when `owner.isNew()` and no customerCode yet)\n- loads all owners; assigns **customerCode** (`assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `CustomerCodes.build` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, HASH8 = SHA-256 of telephone+lastName)\n- assigns **namesakeCount** (case-insensitive first+last matches) and **householdMemberCount**\n- assigns **possibleDuplicate** (`PossibleDuplicates.matchIn`, which always returns null)\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` persists it. At flush, **Hibernate re-validates the entity**: `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone and `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (E.164) on telephone.\n\n## 8. Post-save side-effects\n- **AUDIT log line** written (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`).\n- `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived response fields: displayName, initials, membershipNumber/points/level, locality, contactPreference, identityKey, Luhn checkDigit, ageBand, possibleDuplicate, telephoneDisplay.\n- **`OwnerBulkSignupAdvice`** (`beforeBodyWrite`): sets `bulkSignupWarning=true` if >80 owners created today (informational; never rejects).\n- Returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Two things worth flagging:** the `@PreAuthorize` on the endpoint is not enforced in the default config, and `OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice` reads `sharesHousehold` from raw JSON even though `OwnerFieldsDto` has no such field \u2014 so the household-duplicate bypass can only be triggered via an extra JSON property the DTO silently ignores.\n\nWant me to double-check any specific advice's logic or the exact HTTP status/exception mappings?"
